"Our great inspirer and guide, Saint Philaret the Confessor!",
"Most Blessed Father of ours, bless us, and rejoice always!",
"We received your reply to our brother Peter, which you had the kindness to share with us as well. I do not know when or what our chosen and very dear brother, the professor of the University of Patras, Petros Koutsoukos, wrote to You (note: he is among the foremost university professors of Chemistry in the world, 14th in the world), since he did not make his letter known to me.",
"With much love and esteem for Your venerable person, but also with the fear of God and unceasing prayer night and day, as You know very well, I compose these lines.",
"All the Holy Fathers, with their teaching, the Holy Canons, and the decisions of the Ecumenical and Pan-Orthodox Synods, con-",
"demn equivocal behaviors in matters of Orthodoxy, and anathematize and depose those who consort, fraternize, mingle and wallow together with the harlot heresy, which is represented in every way by the Arch-Ecumenist Athenagoras of Ilion, who at the same time also preaches the abominable heresy of Despotocracy.1 With this great Ecumenist, Chrysostomos Maniotis of Attica consorted, fraternized, mingled and wallowed. And since the Gospel of our Lord commands (Gospel according to Matthew 5:37, in the Sermon on the Mount): “But let your word be Yes, yes; No, no: for whatsoever is more than these cometh of evil” (Matt. 5:37), and in the parallel passage, in the Epistle of James 5:12, the divine Apostle exhorts us: “But let your yea be yea; and your nay, nay; lest ye fall into hypocrisy”, therefore, with anguish of soul and with much love and filial devotion toward Your Beatitude, I gather the teachings of the Holy Fathers and of the holy Canons and set them before You, so that You may take them seriously into account and, with the acuteness that distinguishes You, embrace them and reconsider what You have written, conforming to the spirit and the truth of our God-bearing Teachers:",
