"In Your reply, Most Blessed Father of ours, You try pastorally to balance matters, as is readily gathered from what You have written. But You clearly incline toward the view that this is a matter of courtesy and social decorum and a social protocol of conduct, as regards the repetition of the events, Orthodoxly to be disapproved even in the recent past, of which the instigator, cause and executor was Chrysostomos Maniotis of Attica!",
