"“According to this Canon, no Orthodox Christian ought to receive the gifts which Jews and heretics send to them when they keep their feasts, but neither ought he to celebrate feasts together with them at all. See also the 45th and 70th Apostolic Canons.”",
"“Question. How is it written concerning the heretics, that ‘I hated them that hate thee, O Lord’? And elsewhere it is said, ‘Hate them as enemies of God.’ And again elsewhere, ‘Thou shalt not hate any man’?” And the answer follows: “The heretics, as blasphemers and enemies of God, Scripture did not call men, but dogs and wolves and swine and antichrists…” And immediately comes the decisive phrase:",
"“These, therefore, one must not love, nor associate with, nor pray with, nor eat with, nor receive into the house, nor bid them ‘rejoice’; lest we share in their evil works.” What does “associate with” (<i>syndyazein</i>) mean? The verb <i>syndyazo</i> here must not be restricted to the modern Greek sense “to combine two things.” It has the meaning of being joined, of associating closely, of being coupled, of coming into close communion with someone. Thus a climax is created: neither to associate → nor to pray together → nor to eat together → nor to receive into the house → nor to bid them “rejoice.” And the great Saint and writer Ephraim the Syrian immediately gives the reason:",
"“lest we share in their evil works”, but also so that the Canon of the Church may not be confused, according to all the Fathers of the Church. The Saint’s last phrase obviously refers to 2 John 10–11: “for he that biddeth him God speed is partaker of his evil deeds.” Page 235 of the text of the Work of Saint Ephraim. The digital form preserves the old page numbers. The complete “By Question and Answer” is in the Digital Patrology. E. Beck (ed.), Des heiligen Ephraem des Syrers Hymnen contra Haereses, CSCO 169–170, Scriptores Syri 76–77, Louvain 1957.",
"The Bishop of Attica, Chrysostomos Maniotis, not only received the festal gifts sent by the heretical New Calendarist and Ecumenist, but did even more: he gave CORRESPONDING gifts to the Ecumenist New Calendarist Athenagoras and celebrated ritually together with him, fraternizing, consorting, wallowing and mingling with him! This is an act and an action greater than joint prayer with Athenagoras of Ilion, who is, according to the Holy Canons, a heretical Ecumenist New Calendarist, anathematized by the Synodikon of Orthodoxy and by the anathema of 1998 of our Synod. See also the Synodikon of Orthodoxy:",
"“....as those, then, already rotten, who have cut themselves off from the common body of the Church, ANATHEMA (thrice).” Consequently, as those already rotted by Heresy and cut off by their own will from the Body of the Church, ANATHEMA (thrice). “…to those, then, who irretrievably are held by this error and have their ears stopped against every divine word and spiritual teaching, as those already rotten who have cut themselves off from the common body of the Church, anathema (thrice).” SYNODIKON OF ORTHODOXY (§ 34)",
"THE GOD-BEARING FATHERS TEACH: BEWARE — BEWARE. THOSE WHO ATTEND CHURCH AMONG TODAY’S ECUMENIST NEW CALENDARISTS, SUCH AS THEIR FALSE BISHOPS, ACCORDING TO CANON 15 OF THE FIRST-SECOND SYNOD, AND COMMUNE FROM THEM, A R E D E F I L E D. THEY ARE DARKENED AND HAVE NO ABILITY TO SEPARATE GOOD FROM EVIL, THE RIGHT FROM THE PROFANE, ORTHODOXY FROM HERESY. FLEE FROM THEM, COME OUT FROM AMONG THEM, WALL YOURSELVES OFF AND TOUCH NOT THE UNCLEAN.",
