"A first step of love….",
"Post published: 28 April 2024. By Sotiris M. Tzoumas",
"Today, on Palm Sunday itself, we lived a historic moment. After 100 whole years of discord, hatred, oppositions, divisions and mutual tearing apart, two enlightened representatives of the two sides made the difference and took the first step of love and acceptance, with mutual respect for each other’s beliefs.",
"From what you are reading, some may perhaps consider me an incurable romantic! Yes, I may be.. but I am not an unbeliever! And much less am I a fanatic and intolerant.",
"Today in the square of Saint Blasios in Acharnes, during the Palm Sunday procession that the active and creative Right Reverend Metropolitan of Attica and Boeotia (GOC), Mr. Chrysostomos, holds every year with great success in the streets of the town of Acharnes, a historic meeting took place. The Right Reverend Metropolitan of Ilion, Mr. Athenagoras, an enlightened and open-minded Hierarch, was waiting in the surroundings of Saint Blasios with the Archpriestly Vicar of the Metropolis, Fr. Ioannis, and his Archdeacon, Fr. Nikodemos. As were many faithful who were waiting to venerate the Panagia Tricherousa, who was being carried in procession with honor through the streets of the town for the blessing of the faithful and the town.",
"Chrysostomos and Athenagoras exchanged a kiss of love, and Chrysostomos symbolically gave Athenagoras the arrangement of palm branches that he was holding, and Athenagoras offered him something similar. At the same time the Right Reverend of Ilion kissed the icon of the Panagia Tricherousa — a faithful copy of the one kept at the Holy Monastery of Chilandari on Mount Athos.",
"This historic icon was offered by Mr. Kostas Loulis (former Governor of Mount Athos), who was present at the procession. The icon of the Panagia will be from this evening in the magnificent church — an architectural jewel — of Panagia Soumela in Aspropyrgos, the like of which exists nowhere else in Greece.",
"The people received this peaceful meeting with acclamations and enthusiasm. And it is the second time this has happened. Since last year the two Hierarchs began this meeting, which in the eyes of the faithful constitutes a great step toward historic reconciliation.",
"This is the Church we want… One that keeps our traditions and has love. Besides, the brethren of the old calendar are not heretics! We have no dogmatic differences with them. They are flesh of our flesh. The calendar difference was what once armed the faithful with fanaticism — on both sides — and things were done of which our Church should not be proud. A gravestone must someday be placed over all this. And today a small stone was laid.",
"In the age we live in, we see in the official Church a crowding and competition over who will be photographed with the heterodox, we watch joint prayers of Orthodox with papists, we see Orthodox Hierarchs being photographed and taking part in albums with priestesses and bishopesses of other denominations.",
"And we accept all these things without protest, but they do not give us rest.",
"What happened today in the square of Saint Blasios in Acharnes is a comforting message. Fortunately it seems that there is still hope. It would be good to correct the mistakes of the past on both sides, for the good of all Greek Orthodox.",
"Warm congratulations are due to Metropolitan Chrysostomos for his significant initiative of holding this procession every year on such a day, in remembrance of the procession held in Jerusalem at our Orthodox Patriarchate.",
"And the massive participation of the faithful proves that it has succeeded and is awaited every year by the faithful people. Double congratulations are due to Metropolitan Athenagoras, who, overcoming the ossifications and fanaticisms of the past, attended in this discreet manner an ecclesiastical procession held in order to honor the common leader of our faith, our Lord Jesus Christ, and became the cause for a first page of love to be written after 100 years of discord. Bravo! Yes, there is hope.",
