"-With his continuous heretical moves and his unrepentant stance, and also his continual relapses, he corrupts and weakens the Orthodox Confessional protest and witness. -He has exposed and continually exposes the Orthodox Church, because his actions were and are uncanonical and anti-Orthodox, in the sense that they offend dogmatic Canons of the Church (as our Romanian brethren stress!). See Canons 37 of Laodicea, 6 of Laodicea, 45 and 70 of the Holy Apostles, which classify him among the Ecumenists and the New Calendarists; but above all, his moves and his stance constitute a grave matter of betrayal of the Orthodox Faith and of calling the Orthodox Confession into question. His transgressions are transgressions concerning the Faith, and not some simple canonical violations that might, to some extent, perhaps be excused. -Mr. Chrysostomos is indifferent to the stigma he gives by his stance and teaches anti-Orthodox things, absolving the heresy of Ecumenism of guilt and nullifying the preaching of protest and of the Orthodox Confession.",
