"WE REJECT, CONDEMN AND ANATHEMATIZE: - Everything that the preaching of the Church, the Holy Apostles and the Holy Fathers of the Church rejected, condemned and anathematized, without adding or removing anything. -Those who alter or falsify the texts of the Nicene-Constantinopolitan Creed and of Holy Scripture, as well as those who misinterpret them in a mistaken manner not in accordance with Tradition, as blasphemers and opposers of the Holy Spirit. -Any distortion and any innovation in the Orthodox Tradition. - Those who ever wrote and preached against the right faith (anathema 13 – Council IV), if they have not conformed by the end of their lives. - Ecumenism, which is the heresy of all heresies, and we consider that all the decisions of the Orthodox Synods that have condemned this heresy are in force — the most important being the anathema of the 1983 Synod of the Russian Orthodox Church Outside of Russia (ROCOR), under the leadership of Saint Metropolitan Philaret, and its repetition by the Synod of the Old Orthodox Church of Romania in 2013. As a result of the heresy of Ecumenism, we consider that the “churches” that have adopted, support (or continue to support), or are unwilling to condemn Ecumenism, as well as those in communion with them (clergy or laity), have fallen from the One Church and the True Faith and their ministry lacks Holy Grace. All their judgments, therefore, we consider as not belonging to the Church, and we regard their members as heretics, because of Ecumenism, and schismatics, because of the rejection of the Julian calendar of the Holy Fathers. - Any form of recognition of the sacraments of heretics and schismatics, regardless of who makes it and when. - The Encyclical of the Patriarchate of Constantinople of 1920, titled “To all the Churches of Christ everywhere”. - The calendar reform decided by the so-called Pan-Orthodox Congress of 1923, which falls under the condemnation of the three Pan-Orthodox Synods of the 16th century — we consider that it constitutes an application of the heresy of Ecumenism and consequently also a schism. - The founding and the whole work of the World Council of Churches and of all its members.",
"- Sergianism, as a heresy that teaches that the Church must submit to the atheistic, secularized and anti-Christian state. - Freemasonry and organizations similar to it, as organizations hostile to the Church, and participation in them by any member, cleric or lay, of our Church is forbidden. - The heresy known as the “Theory of the diseased member”, as well as the work entitled “Ecclesiological Positions”, whose authors and unrepentant supporters essentially claim that the Ecumenist heretics are members of the One, Holy, Sovereign and Apostolic Church until a Great Synod is proclaimed and decides it. Thus all forms of this heresy are also condemned, including the expression of the idea that the Ecumenist heretics (or heretics in general) can be in the One, Holy, Sovereign and Apostolic Church until a Great Synod is convened to pronounce their condemnation. - Those who consider the Ecumenist, neo-Calvinist and Sergianist “churches” to be Orthodox and possessing Holy Grace, - Those who administer to heretics and schismatics the Mystery of the Divine Eucharist, as if it were useful for their salvation, - Those who have drawn up and support the non-Orthodox teaching called the “theory of the sick member”, which is expressed chiefly in the writing of the text of the “Ecclesiological Positions”, - All who believe that the Apostolicity of the Church and of its Hierarchs is not complete. - The theories concerning the appearance and evolution of the universe and of the species, since we believe that God brought the whole world, visible and invisible (the world of the angels), into being out of non-being (Genesis, chapters 1 and 2), and that man is a creation of God in His image and likeness (Genesis 1:27). IN CONCLUSION, WE SAY TO ALL THOSE WHO: - Turn against Holy Scripture or Holy Tradition, distorting their meaning, - Do not believe in God, do not accept the Divinity of the Savior Jesus Christ, do not honor the Mother of God, the Precious Cross and all the Saints recognized by the Universal Orthodox Church, - Attack the Nicene-Constantinopolitan Creed, both in its wording and in its meanings, - Do not respect the dogmatic and canonical decisions of the Ecumenical and Local Councils recognized by the Fullness of the Church, - Do not honor the Holy Icons and the Holy Relics, - Regard heretics as part, or as being able to be part, of the Church of Christ,",
