"To the Holy Synod of the G.O.C. of Greece (which is under His Beatitude",
"Archbishop Kallinikos), in respect for Your institutional mission and in",
"the hope of a confessional clarification, a word of conscience is submitted.",
" Being informed with grief of what is taking place in the Orthodox Mission of Indonesia, and as an expression of the deepest love toward the Church and the Synod, we venture the present letter as a voice of pastoral vigilance and ecclesiological discernment.",
" Invoking the example of the Holy Fathers and the boldness of the Confessors, we expect a synodal position from the Synod, as protectress of the Orthodox mind of the Church.",
" Within this framework, there follows a brief record of the ecclesiastical course of the Church of Indo-",
" nesia, as the basis of a theological consideration and pastoral approach.",
" Section A – Introduction and historical framework of the Church of Indonesia",
" Summary of the historical course",
" 1. The Church of Indonesia was founded in 1991, following the missionary impulse of Fr. Daniel Biantoro, a Muslim, who converted to Orthodoxy on the occasion of the book “The Orthodox Church” by Bishop Kallistos Ware. After his ordination (1985–87) by the Ecumenical Patriarchate, he returned to Indonesia, where the nucleus of the local Orthodox Community was founded.",
" During his administrative course within the Metropolis of Hong Kong (1996–2004), which was under the guidance of Metropolitan Nikitas Lulias, significant disputes arose regarding questions of canonicity and the management of Church property. These led to the deposition of Biantoro by the Ecumenical Patriarch.",
" In the year 2005, the Russian Orthodox Church Outside of Russia (ROCOR) received Fr. Daniel Biantoro, and Metropolitan Hilarion of the Russians of the Diaspora ordained him Archimandrite (<i>cheirothesia</i>), marking a new page in his course.",
" In 2019, the Church of Indonesia came over to the Genuine Greek Orthodox Church of the G.O.C. of Greece; this transition does not appear to have taken place on a firm theological basis, but most probably occurred for administrative reasons, related to the wish of the flock for a more Indonesian and self-governing Church.",
" In 2023, Fr. Daniel Biantoro was ordained Bishop of Nikopolis (Jakarta), completing a course of personal and administrative movement.",
" In conclusion it is observed that the coming of the Church of Indonesia to the Church of the G.O.C. of Greece is not inferred to be an act of dogmatic confession, but an administrative quest for freedom of movement and local management.",
" Next, for a fuller documentation of the picture and the course of the Church of Indonesia, a brief chronological report is set out on the publicly performed and officially recorded events.",
" 2. On 24 December 2023, Fr. Timothy Tomi, as representative of the Church of Indonesia in a certain district of Jakarta, attended an event titled: “Visit to Churches at Christmas”, with the Deputy Governor of the area and other religious leaders. The event included visits to three Churches of heterodox confessions (Roman Catholic, Protestant and Calvinist).",
" During his address, Mr. Timothy took a public position preaching that “diversity is our strength,” putting forward love and brotherhood among the heterodox as an axiom, as the center of spiritual understanding. This phrase clearly accords with the slogan of contemporary Ecumenism, “unity in diversity,” which focuses on a superficial coexistence of dogmas, bypassing the necessary dogmatic unity of the Orthodox Faith.",
" 3. On 18 January 2024, Father Jacob, General President of the Orthodox Church of Indonesia, attended and officially participated, together with state officials and representatives of the regional government of Central Kalimantan, in an inauguration ceremony of the National Committee for Pascha 2024, which was held in a hotel. The event was characterized by a spirit of enthusiasm, hope and interreligious understanding, within the framework of a conference with public bodies of various faiths, with the aim of a common celebration of Pascha at the national level.",
" At the ceremony, Father Jacob officially took part in a public joint prayer, as is evident in the attached photograph, together with the state officials and representatives of heterodox communities, and indeed with the palms of his hands turned downward.",
"  This position of the hands is encountered in pagan religions, where worship is directed to chthonic deities — such as Hades, king of the underworld, Persephone, Charon, the Erinyes and other dark figures of ancient mythology.",
" The direction of the hands downward (toward the depth of the earth) carries the symbolism of invoking the powers of the underworld, and does not accord with the anagogical nature of Orthodox prayer, which is expressed by the lifting of the hands toward heaven, as a sign of supplication, hope and communion with God.",
