"Wednesday 24 March 2010",
"An Archimandrite… of Mykonos for the Metropolis of Ilion is revealed by Eleftheri Ora!",
"Some things are not accidental. In the climate of… licentiousness that prevails in Greek society everything is possible, even the fact that the Archbishop’s Chosen One for the Metropolis of Ilion, Mr. ATHENAGORAS DIKAIAKOS (photograph), strolls in civilian clothes through the streets of Mykonos, as “Eleftheri Ora tis Kyriakis” revealed! It seems that many young clerics, fortunately not all, have not realized their mission, nor the obligations that derive from their ministry. They believe that they are ordinary people and can act and behave like the rest. Unfortunately, these clerics come from the ranks of the unmarried.",
"One such is Archimandrite Athenagoras Dikaiakos, a protégé of the Archbishop, who destines him to be the shepherd of the New Metropolis of Ilion. This cleric, in the summer months, likes to visit resorts of licentiousness, having cast off the cassock. The camera lens caught him, as you see in the photograph, in Mykonos. Here some further questions arise for the Archimandrite: Is there a regular presence of his in Arachova? For what reasons did he leave the monastery of Sagmatas in Livadeia? Does he handle the Press matters for Mr. Ieronymos from the time of Boeotia?"
